SAP / ABAP Work 

Review functional specifications, draft TSDs, explain code, prepare debugging steps and generate test scenarios. 

11. Prompt Review Checklist 

Is the task specific enough? 

Is the audience clearly mentioned? 

Is enough context provided? 

Are constraints and exclusions clear? 

Is the output format defined? 

Are examples provided when consistency is required? 

Are facts, assumptions and uncertainties separated? 

Is the final answer reviewed before use? 

12. 30-Day Learning Roadmap 

Timeline 

Focus Area 

Week 1 

Learn AI basics, Generative AI, LLMs and common limitations. Practice simple prompts daily. 

Week 2 

Practice role, task, context, constraints and output formats. Build 10 reusable prompt templates. 

Week 3 

Learn few-shot prompting, prompt chaining, verification prompts and document-based prompting. 

Week 4 

Explore RAG, AI agents, prompt security and one practical business use case from your project. 

13. Golden Rules 

Be specific about the task. 

Provide enough context for the AI to make the right decision. 

Use examples when the required style or format matters. 

Ask for structured output such as tables, bullets or templates. 

Break large tasks into smaller steps. 

Ask the AI to verify important facts and assumptions. 

Review results critically before business or technical use. 

Continuously improve your prompt based on the output quality. 

Appendix: Reusable Master Templates 

Detailed Analysis Template 

Act as a senior [role]. Analyze the following [document/code/process]. Identify objective, key points, gaps, risks, assumptions and recommended next steps. Return the output in a structured format with headings and bullet points. 

 

Professional Email Template 

Draft a polite and professional email for [audience]. Context: [context]. Message to convey: [message]. Tone: simple, human and professional. Keep it concise and include a clear next step. 

 

Technical Specification Template 

Act as a senior technical architect. Create a technical specification for [object/interface/report]. Include purpose, scope, assumptions, input/output, process flow, validations, error handling, security, performance, test scenarios and deployment notes. 

 


 
